.TH JONBOY 1 "2026-11-13" "JonBoy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jonboy \- PlayStation 1 (R3000A) emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jonboy
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jonboy --headless
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jonboy --exe
.I file.exe
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jonboy --boot
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jonboy --bench
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jonboy --gdb
.RI [ port ]
.br
.B jonboy --savestate-selftest
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jonboy
is a PlayStation 1 emulator written in C and rendered with SDL3. It boots the
retail BIOS and runs games from a mounted disc image, with a software GPU, SPU
audio, a DualShock controller, and memory cards. It also supports an invented
PSIO-style SD-card cartridge and an in-emulation loader menu.
.PP
With no mode flag,
.B jonboy
opens an SDL window and starts the CPU at the BIOS reset vector
.RB ( 0xBFC00000 ).
If no BIOS is given it maps
.I bios.bin
from the working directory when present. The picture is always presented at the
4:3 format the console sends to a TV, independent of the game's internal
horizontal resolution.
.SH MODES
.TP
.BI --headless " file"
Load a flat binary into RAM and run it without a window. On stop it prints the
registers, \fB$s0\fR, and a memory window.
.TP
.BI --exe " file.exe"
Load and run a PlayStation executable (PS-EXE) headless. Used by the conformance
runner, which reads a PASS or FAIL verdict back from the framebuffer.
.TP
.B --boot
Boot the BIOS headless.
.TP
.B --bench
Run the deterministic core unpaced and report the emulation thread's wall time
per emulated frame against the 16.67 ms budget.
.TP
.BI --gdb " [port]"
Boot the BIOS headless and wait for a GDB remote connection on a loopback TCP
socket (default port 1234). The CPU starts halted at the reset vector.
.TP
.B --savestate-selftest
Boot headless, save state, then prove a reload reproduces the next run
bit-for-bit. \fB--steps\fR sets the warmup depth.
.TP
.BI --sideload " file.exe"
Boot the BIOS, then swap in a PS-EXE once the kernel reaches the shell entry.
Implies \fB--boot\fR.
.SH BOOT OPTIONS
These apply to the windowed emulator and to
.BR --boot .
.TP
.BI --bios " file"
BIOS image to load (default
.IR bios.bin ).
.TP
.BI --cd " file"
Mount a disc image: a
.IR .bin ,
.IR .cue
(including multi-track), or
.IR .iso .
.TP
.BI --memcard " file"
Slot 1 memory card image, a raw 128 KB file created and formatted if absent.
.TP
.BI --memcard2 " file"
Slot 2 memory card image, same format as
.BR --memcard .
.TP
.BI --games " dir"
Directory the loader menu browses. In the windowed build this auto-loads the
menu, navigated with the pad.
.TP
.BI --script " file"
Run a timed system-event script that drives the pad, analog mode, and disc
insert or eject, keyed by the video frame counter.
.TP
.B --psio
Inject the PSIO boot stub over the BIOS entry.
.TP
.BI --sd " file"
Mount a virtual SD-card image for the PSIO cartridge.
.TP
.BI --firmware " file"
Load a PSIO firmware ROM image.
.SH BENCHMARK OPTIONS
Used with
.BR --bench .
.TP
.BI --bench-warmup " n"
Frames to run before measuring (default 300).
.TP
.BI --bench-frames " n"
Frames to measure (default 600, about 10 s of console time).
.SH HEADLESS AND CAPTURE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --load-addr " hex"
Physical load address for
.B --headless
(default 0).
.TP
.BI --pc " hex"
Entry PC (default is the load address).
.TP
.BI --steps " n"
Maximum instructions to run.
.TP
.BI --vram-out " file"
Write the visible 320x240 framebuffer region as a PPM image at the end of a run.
.TP
.BI --frames-out " dir"
Write a numbered framebuffer PPM into
.I dir
periodically during a boot run, producing a filmstrip.
.TP
.BI --frames-every " n"
Dump one frame every
.I n
video frames (default 30).
.TP
.BI --frames-from " n"
First video frame to start dumping at (default 0).
.SH CONTROLS
In the windowed build the keyboard drives the pad: the arrow keys are the D-pad;
.BR Z ", " X ", " A ", " S
are Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle;
.B Enter
and
.B Right Shift
are Start and Select;
.BR Q ", " W ", " E ", " R
are L1, R1, L2, R2;
.B C
and
.B V
are L3 and R3; and
.B Tab
toggles the DualShock analog mode. A connected SDL gamepad drives the buttons and
both analog sticks.
.B Escape
opens the menu overlay, and
.B F1
toggles between the display area and the full 1024x512 VRAM view.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JONBOY_GPU_THREAD
Set to
.B 0
to disable the GPU rasterization worker thread and fall back to inline
rasterization.
.TP
.B JONBOY_PERF
Set to
.B 1
to force the performance HUD on at startup.
.TP
.B JONBOY_AUDIO_CUSHION_MS
Override the audio run-ahead cushion in milliseconds.
.B 0
disables the run-ahead and leaves pure real-time pacing.
.TP
.B JONBOY_FASTTICK
Override the per-step hardware tick batching. The real-time windowed build
enables it; the deterministic modes leave it off for exact per-instruction
behavior.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the configuration file. See FILES.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I bios.bin
BIOS image mapped from the working directory when no
.B --bios
is given.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jonboy/jonboy.ini
Persisted window, view, audio, and controller settings. Falls back to
.I ~/.config/jonboy/jonboy.ini
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.SH EXAMPLES
Boot a game through a retail BIOS from a mounted disc:
.PP
.RS
.nf
jonboy --bios scph5501.bin --cd Game.cue
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a PS-EXE conformance test and save its framebuffer:
.PP
.RS
.nf
jonboy --exe CPUADD.exe --vram-out add.ppm
.fi
.RE
.PP
Browse a games directory from the on-screen loader menu:
.PP
.RS
.nf
jonboy --games /path/to/games --bios scph5501.bin
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and
.I TODO.md
document the subsystems, test suites, and current status in detail.
